I've never had the patience for thown weapons, personaly. I usualy get
burdend, and ammo is the first thing to go... Plus I've always had
trouble managing my quiver.

I guess I should turn autoquiver on... I'd forgotten about it until
now, and that's probibly why I get so frustrated with fired weapons. I
run out of ammo, and hate dealing with that one arrow/dagger/dart in my
inventory.

I supose for people like me who don't like to deal with ammo, it's a
usefull strategy, especialy since it seems to work w/o speed boots,
just w/o any margin for error. If you take you're time with it, it
souldn't cause any problems. Even in the unlikely case you do hit a
polymorph trap(or more likely a beartrap or a pit) or the cockatrice
starts moving faster, you usualy have some way of getting away
(Elbereth, teleportation, wands...)

I will admit that I don't want to use it without a lizard corpse handy.



